# Feelings in Russian: мне ску́чно
subtitle: "Say how you feel in Russian: мне ску́чно, гру́стно, ве́село, стра́шно, интере́сно; ему́ and ей for others; and я рад, glad to see you."
tags: ["russian","russian feelings","emotions","мне скучно","russian vocabulary"]
teaches: ["vocabulary/feelings","grammar/to-ending"]
thumb: "band \"Bored? Say мне\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Time words in Russian: уже́, ещё, че́рез","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/85-russian-time-words.cast"}

